Since April, people have reported bookings landing on the wrong day. The desk merged the
reports into #4471. The export has overlapping rows, so repeated report IDs are counted once.

The reports describe two causes. The shared parser reads every date month first, so it flips
dates for day-first tenants. Separately, booking-v3 tells people to enter month first while
the form interprets their input in the tenant's day-first locale. These need separate fixes.

<Callout>
Known reports, split by cause below. Counts use unique report IDs and the tenant's configured
locale and form, not the intake tag or subject line.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Follow-up issues

- Parser: [Parse dates in the tenant's locale](https://github.com/Kaggee/mega-challenges/issues/1).
- Booking-v3 hint: [Match the date hint to the tenant locale](https://github.com/Kaggee/mega-challenges/issues/2).

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Triage notes

- **Parser:** This cause spans the tenants and reports from app, email, and form.
- **Booking-v3 hint:** This cause appears in Alder Physio, Copper Studio, and Pale Harbour;
  these reports arrived through the form.
- Intake tags do not determine the cause. The tenant locale and booking form do.
- The desk flags some reports as one-day moves. The supplied classifier assigns them to parser
  by tenant; their narratives still need review before treating them as fully explained.

## Lessons

- A large merged ticket can contain more than one bug. Classify by tenant configuration and
  report path before filing issues.
- Deduplicate overlapping exports by report ID before counting.
- Write the page while the queue is still in your head.

